      "mergeID": "665dc6bab8154ee35a0e67b9",
      "mergedPostDetails": "A few days after the 2024.2.2 update, overall performance dropped drastically. It is hard to pinpoint, but after the update, performance has major spikes in VR mode during these cases:\n\n-Facing towards mirrors\n\n-Facing towards media players\n\n-Having more than 2 or 3 players in the instance\n\nIt also happens with playtime itself. The game becomes unplayable after just a couple of world loads. Which leads to the suspicion of all this being caused by a memory leak from the update. I am an AMD user, so maybe the update broke things further for me instead of fixing them as stated in the update notes.\n\nAlready did a clean reinstallation of VRC. Same problems persist.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Horrible performance after update",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "66567edf3ec872d7571edc78",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Specs: AMD Ryzen 3 3200U with Radeon Vega Mobile Gfx. 20 GB (17.9 usable) RAM, 2 GB VRAM. Game has been running perfectly fine in VR mode up until this point. Already looking to seeing if theres a way to assign higher VRAM for the card to use.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
