      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "And another update: In Desktop mode, game is in the 50-60 fps range in optimized worlds (the one I have as my home is Ramu's Gun Range, where I am testing this). It does take a dip down to 30 in VR mode but stays stable. However, player presence still messes up the performance. I know for a fact now that avatars don't matter, as the slowdowns and delays occur no matter where I am looking. Game is perfectly fine in the desktop window but delayed in the headset, so maybe its an encoder issue?",
